From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: let the host refuse an executable

A Worker cannot compile code at run time, so the host runs only the
executables it holds a build of. start_thread() handed the new image
to the host with no way to say no, and the host's only answer to an
unknown hash was to throw, which took the whole machine down with the
one process. wasm_load_executable() now returns nonzero to refuse, and
load_wasm_binary() calls it before finalize_exec(). The exec is past
its point of no return by then, so a refused exec kills the process
with SIGSEGV, as any late exec failure does.
---
 arch/wasm/include/asm/wasm.h |  2 +-
 arch/wasm/kernel/process.c   |  3 ---
 fs/binfmt_wasm.c             | 10 ++++++++++
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/include/asm/wasm.h b/arch/wasm/include/asm/wasm.h
index a9b032f6d..2490ea04e 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/include/asm/wasm.h
+++ b/arch/wasm/include/asm/wasm.h
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ extern void wasm_release_task(struct task_struct *dead_task);
 extern struct task_struct *wasm_serialize_tasks(struct task_struct *prev_task,
 	struct task_struct *next_task);
 
-extern void wasm_load_executable(unsigned long bin_start, unsigned long bin_end,
+extern int wasm_load_executable(unsigned long bin_start, unsigned long bin_end,
 	unsigned long data_start, unsigned long table_start);
 extern void wasm_reload_program(void);
 
diff --git a/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c b/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c
index ee5bee34e..ac4cd4611 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/wasm/kernel/process.c
@@ -269,9 +269,6 @@ void start_thread(struct pt_regs *regs, unsigned long stack_pointer)
 	regs->stack_pointer = stack_pointer;
 	regs->cpuflags = CPUFLAGS_USER_TASK_DEFAULT;
 
-	wasm_load_executable(current->mm->start_code, current->mm->end_code,
-		current->mm->start_data, 0U);
-
 	/* Reload the program when the current syscall exits. */
 	current_thread_info()->flags |= _TIF_RELOAD_PROGRAM;
 }
diff --git a/fs/binfmt_wasm.c b/fs/binfmt_wasm.c
index 508c953b2..be527d3d9 100644
--- a/fs/binfmt_wasm.c
+++ b/fs/binfmt_wasm.c
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@
 #include <linux/uaccess.h>
 #include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 
+#include <asm/wasm.h>
+
 /*
  * 128 KiB with the argument page, binfmt_elf_fdpic's default for nommu programs. Without an MMU a
  * stack is committed memory, so the host grows it in segments up to RLIMIT_STACK as the program
@@ -441,6 +443,14 @@ static int load_wasm_binary(struct linux_binprm *bprm)
 	if (res)
 		return res;
 
+	/*
+	 * The host refuses code it holds no build of. That is past the point
+	 * of no return, so exec kills the process with SIGSEGV.
+	 */
+	if (wasm_load_executable(current->mm->start_code, current->mm->end_code,
+			current->mm->start_data, 0U))
+		return -ENOEXEC;
+
 	finalize_exec(bprm);
 	start_thread(regs, current->mm->start_stack);
 
-- 
2.43.0

